As GRC and Compliance Officer for this migration programme, I have reviewed the Workload Sovereignty Profile for the Sovereign Health application and identified three primary concerns that require resolution before I can endorse the migration plan.

First, the data classification pass has flagged NHS patient records -- including patient identifiers, diagnoses, and medical histories -- as high-severity findings. The proposed landing zone is an EU-sovereign provider (Open Telekom Cloud), but I need written confirmation that all data residency controls explicitly restrict patient data to UK/EEA storage with no backup replication outside these jurisdictions.

